karr #161 / docs/adr/0048 compiles the two rule regexes with `use re "/a"`, which is the perl 5.14 form of the `re` pragma. cpanfile line 1 still says:

    requires 'perl', '5.010';

On 5.10 lib/File/SOPS/Metadata.pm no longer compiles, so the declared floor is now a false claim rather than a conservative one. Nothing else in lib was found needing more than 5.10, so 5.014 is the honest floor.

cpanfile is outside the api lane's files and outside the file boundary karr #161 was given, which is why this is a ticket and not part of that change. One line:

    requires 'perl', '5.014';

Worth checking the same run whether any dependency already raises it higher.
ERLEDIGT 2026-08-21 im selben Commit ebfb1e3, weil es dorthin gehoerte: use re '/a' braucht perl 5.014, das cpanfile versprach 5.010. Ein Release ohne diese Zeile haette auf einem perl installiert, auf dem das Modul nicht kompiliert. Verifiziert: /a wurde in 5.014 eingefuehrt.
